& [ExportedFixtureAndLedgerCandidateSet] is the future fixture proof boundary exported by IR2
  + [fixture_source_root] is tests/fixtures/sop/ir2_parser_projection/
  + [fixture_expected_root] is tests/fixtures/expected/ir2_parser_projection/
  + [fixture_generated_root] is tests/fixtures/generated/ir2_parser_projection/
  + [fixture_case_set] is valid_signed_canonical_artifact, source_only_unprocessed_artifact, missing_signature_canonical_artifact, wrong_protocol_signature, stale_source_hash, malformed_sop_structure, unresolved_natural_key, broken_lineage, generated_projection_non_authority, and source_mutation_refusal
  + [expected_ledger_shape_set] is ExpectedKernelRecordLedgerShape, ExpectedSQLiteProjectionLedgerShape, and ExpectedValidationLedgerShape
  + [fixture_status] is candidate_only_until_explicit_activation

  = must: track fixture source and expected ledgers as reviewable SOP material when a future activation slice creates them
  = must: keep generated fixture outputs disposable and non-authoritative

& [AuthorityProjectionBoundary] is the source/projection authority boundary exported by IR2
  + [source_authority_root] is docs/
  + [tracked_fixture_authority_root] is tests/fixtures/sop/ and tests/fixtures/expected/ only after fixture creation is explicitly activated
  + [generated_projection_root] is .langsop/
  + [generated_test_projection_root] is tests/fixtures/generated/
  + [sqlite_authority_status] is derived_projection_only
  + [langgraph_checkpoint_authority_status] is execution_state_only
  + [surface_state_authority_status] is projection_only
  + [chat_protocol_authority_status] is projection_or_carrier_only

  = must: reject generated SQLite, cache, parser output, LangGraph checkpoint, surface projection, IRC, Matrix, terminal, Codex, or web chat state as source authority unless a future source-preserved and SJS-processed record explicitly imports it
  = must: preserve source mutation refusal as a first implementation proof obligation

& [CodeActivationBoundaryExport] is the activation boundary exported by IR2
  + [code_creation_authorized_by_this_pack] is false
  + [code_creation_precondition_satisfied] is IR2-S01 through IR2-S08 accepted
  + [next_ready_work] is IR2 bounded parser/projection implementation activation surface
  + [next_ready_work_model_route] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [future_bounded_code_route] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after explicit activation selects a bounded implementation slice
  + [deeper_reasoning_required_for] is authority semantics, parser profile, extraction mapping, validation contract, SQLite schema, generated artifact policy, dependency additions, and downstream gate changes

  = must: use a future activation review or minted implementation slice before writing code, creating fixture files, creating expected ledgers, or generating SQLite outputs
  = must: keep implementation completion review mandatory before accepting any code or fixture output

& [DownstreamGateExport] is the downstream readiness boundary exported by IR2
  + [IR3_planning_intake_state] is may_consume_IR2_authority_projection_pack_after_completion_review
  + [IR3_implementation_state] is gated_until_IR2_bounded_parser_projection_implementation_review_is_accepted_or_a_rebake_reclassifies_IR3_scope
  + [IR3_model_route] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable only for bounded operator harness and fixture runner work after required parser/projection proof exists
  + [IR3_deeper_reasoning_required_for] is any change to authority, checkpoint, operator trace, interrupt, or downstream activation semantics
  + [safety_limit] is no live operations control authorized

  = must: prevent a false-ready IR3 implementation signal while allowing downstream planning to cite the accepted IR2 contract pack
  = must: treat a desire to skip IR2 implementation proof as a rebake candidate, not an implicit activation

& [IR2PackInvalidationRuleSet] is the staleness contract for IR2AuthorityProjectionPackV1
  + [invalidated_by] is change to IR2 source manifest, canonical specification, slice surface, or SJS signature basis
  + [invalidated_by] is change to any accepted IR2-S01 through IR2-S07 output hash
  + [invalidated_by] is change to any IR2-S01 through IR2-S08 completion review that affects support, requirements, or gates
  + [invalidated_by] is parser, validation, projection, fixture, generated artifact, or dependency behavior exceeding the exported boundaries
  + [invalidated_by] is generated projection promoted to source authority
  + [invalidated_by] is silent mutation of SOP authority files by parser/projection implementation
  + [invalidated_by] is operations control or live machine control leak

  = must: rerun IR2-S08 or rebake the relevant surface after invalidation before downstream work consumes this pack again
